# Chart colours

Use only these colours in charts and heatmaps. A colour either names a source, such as the dishwasher, or shows an amount, such as energy used. Chart colours do not change with dark mode or the theme colour. The exception is the total consumption line, `civica-chart-9`, which turns White in dark mode.

## Chart palette

<%= colour_copy_status %>

The chart palette has:

<%= colour_group_links('charts') %>

### Categorical palette

Use these 6 colours for sources, such as devices. Use Black tint 80% for axes and grid lines, and Black for labels.

<%= colour_chart_categorical %>

### Sequential and divergent scale palette

Use one colour family to show an amount, light for less and dark for more. For a difference from a target, use two families with a neutral centre. Never blend colours between the listed steps.

<%= colour_groups(colour_page('charts').fetch('sequential'), level: 4, key: 'scale') %>

#### Scale steps from light to dark

Blues have 7 steps and other families have 6.

<%=
  edge = govuk_colour('black-tint-80').fetch('hex')
  families = colour_page('charts').fetch('sequential').map do |group|
    steps = group.fetch('colours').sort_by { |id| -colour_luminance(govuk_colour(id).fetch('hex')) }
    chips = steps.each_with_index.map do |id, index|
      colour = govuk_colour(id)
      short = colour.fetch('name').sub(/\APrimary \w+\z/, 'Primary').sub(/\A(Blue|Magenta|Red|Green|Purple|Teal|Orange|Black) (tint|shade)/) { "#{$2.capitalize}" }
      %(<li style="width:72px;margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.25"><span aria-hidden="true" style="display:block;height:32px;margin-bottom:5px;border:1px solid #{edge};background:#{colour.fetch('hex')}"></span><span class="govuk-visually-hidden">Step #{index + 1}: #{colour.fetch('name')}</span><span aria-hidden="true">#{short}</span></li>)
    end
    %(<h5 style="margin:15px 0 5px">#{escape(group.fetch('title'))}, light to dark</h5><ol class="govuk-list" style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;padding:0;margin:0 0 15px;list-style:none">#{chips.join}</ol>)
  end
  %(<div class="c-colour-example">#{families.join}</div>)
%>

