## Using colour in charts

- Never use colour as the only cue. Give every series a name and a pattern, line style or marker. Offer the data as a table.
- Use as few colours as possible. Let people hide series instead.
- Use no more than 2 colour scales in one chart.
- Check each colour against its background. Orange tint 25% is faint on white. In dark mode, Blue shade 50% (1.2:1) and Primary blue (2.9:1) are hard to see on a card. There, the name or pattern must carry the meaning. [Test combinations and keep another cue](colour.html#bg-col-03) gives the contrast you need.

### Single category

A week of daily electricity use. One measure needs one colour, so every bar is Primary blue.

